  "body": "## Goal\n\nPost more than one independently supported cut in a single native Agie job. Today each contour requires a separate job directory.\n\n## Work\n\nAssign a distinct geometry resource, work and threading point to each contour. Check the shared work coordinate system, stock and technology. Check every lead and compensated path against all retained geometry. Refuse touching contours, dependencies on cut order, unsupported setups and any unaccounted workpiece. Document that the resident controller can group passes across separate works.\n\nDone means: A normal CAMCraft job with two safely separated cuts creates one complete native bundle. The offline controller resolves both geometries, uses the correct starting holes and plots the two independent cuts without a cutting traverse across the stock. An unsafe pair refuses the whole bundle before publication.\n",
